# ld64 symbol pattern list used with -force_symbols_not_weak_list.
#
# Mach-O C++ symbols have one platform-leading underscore plus the Itanium ABI
# `_Z...` mangling, hence `__Z*`.  Making C++ definitions non-weak prevents
# vtable entries from participating in dyld weak coalescing.  The accompanying
# exported-symbols allow-list then keeps those strong definitions private to
# libmithril, so neither Amethyst's libshaderc.dylib nor libmithril can satisfy
# the other image's glslang weak lookups.
__Z*
